# Vercel Speed Insights Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency:** `@vercel/speed-insights` (v2.0.0)
- **Modified:** `frontend/package.json` - Added the Speed Insights package to dependencies
- **Updated:** `frontend/package-lock.json` - Lockfile updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Component Integration
- **Modified:** `frontend/src/App.jsx`
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
  - Wrapped Routes component in a React Fragment (`<>...</>`) to allow multiple root-level elements
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component after the Routes component
  - This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all routes in the application

### 3. Implementation Details
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- The SpeedInsights component is placed at the app root level to capture performance metrics across all routes
- No additional configuration is required; the component will automatically collect and send performance data when deployed on Vercel

### 4. Testing & Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No TypeScript/linting errors introduced
- ✅ Application structure preserved with minimal changes
- ✅ All dependencies properly installed and locked

## Next Steps for Deployment
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Monitor performance metrics in the Vercel Speed Insights dashboard after users visit the site

## Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependencies
- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Integrated SpeedInsights component

The integration follows React and Vite best practices and uses the latest official documentation from Vercel.
